===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One that plays.
## One who plays any game or sport.
##: {{ux|en| He is a '''player''' for the Australian team.}}
##: {{syn|en|laker<q:UK, Ireland dialectal>}}
## {{lb|en|theater}} An [[actor]] in a [[dramatic]] play.
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare As You Like It|act=II|scene=vii|column=1|page=194|passage=All the world's a ſtage, / And all the men and women, merely '''Players'''}}
## {{lb|en|music}} One who plays on a [[musical instrument]].
## {{lb|en|gaming|video games}} A [[gamer]]; a person of video games or similar.
##: {{ux|en| He is an avid Minecraft '''player'''.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=2015|author=Angus Slater|title=Prophecy, Pre-destination, and Free-form Gameplay: The Nerevarine Prophecy in Bethesda’s ‘''Morrowind''’|volume=7|journal=Online: Heidelberg Journal of Religions on the Internet|page=175|doi=10.11588/rel.2015.0.18512|url=https://heiup.uni-heidelberg.de/journals/index.php/religions/article/view/18512|text=The '''player''' is free to create their own narrative within a much larger set of possible designed narrative options, or, given the geographic and dialogical openness of {{w|The Elder Scrolls III: Morrowind|''Morrowind''}}, to refuse the creation of any narrative but their own and wander aimlessly through the game.}}
## {{lb|en|gambling}} A [[gambler]].
## {{lb|en|historical}} A mechanism that [[actuate]]s a [[player piano]] or other automatic musical instrument.
##* {{quote-book|en|title=The Technical History of the '''Player'''|author=John McTammany|year=1915|passage=But up to this time the application of the '''player''' mechanism had been confined to reed instruments, the piano manufacturers having successfully resisted the introduction of the '''player''' mechanism into the piano; but, in the meantime, the manufacturers of '''players''' had grown strong and the manufacturers were beginning to properly interpret the handwriting on the wall}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=Regulation and Repair of Piano and Player Mechanism, ...|page=179|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=CT1BAAAAIAAJ|author=William Braid White|year=1909|passage=A Technical Treatise on Piano Player Mechanism" contains detailed description of the various types of interior and exterior '''players''', embracing manual, pneumatic, automatic, mechanical and electric}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=Player piano: the history of the mechanical piano and how to repair it|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ukE5AQAAIAAJ|author=Arthur W. J. G. Ord-Hume|year=1970|passage=Electric '''players''' used either a four-lobe rotary pump belt-driven by an electric motor or a self-contained electric motor and ...}}
## {{lb|en|electronics}} An electronic device that plays audio or video media.
##: ''Is your CD '''player''' broken, or is this one disc damaged?''
## {{lb|en|computing}} A software application that plays audio or video media, such as a [[media player]].
# One who is [[playful]]; one without serious aims; an [[idler]]; a [[trifler]].
# A [[participant]]; one involved in something.
#: {{ux|en|He thought he could become a '''player''', at least at the state level.}}
#: {{co|en|a major '''player''' in the direct banking sector}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Suzanne Shale|title=Moral Leadership in Medicine|page=239
|passage=Decision realities research recognizes the occupational tribalism identified in occupational realities research, but goes further by paying attention to all the '''players''' – patients and lay caregivers included – who participate in negotiating care.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=November 7, 2012|author=Matt Bai|title=Winning a Second Term, Obama Will Confront Familiar Headwinds|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0
|passage=Another Bush — George W.’s brother Jeb — is likely to be a big '''player''' in the Republican Party’s future.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 March 10|author=Nigel Harris|title=It's time to get on with it!|journal=RAIL|issue=926|page=3|text=As the biggest rail '''player''', Network Rail was usually held accountable for failings, but had no authority to change anything to solve the problems. The DfT had been given that authority in 2004 - but consistently ducked accountability.}}
## One who participates in a particular type of sexual [[play]].
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=22 Apr 91|journal=Gay Community News|page=11|author=Wickie Stamps|title=A Lesbian Looks At The GMSMA's 10<sup>th</sup> Anniversary Celebration|text=In this space we explored lesbian sadomasochism, met other S/M women who were serious '''players''', had access to safe equipment and, through  watching other women, learned new techniques.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A person who [[play the field|plays the field]] rather than having a long-term sexual relationship.
#: {{syn|en|fuck boy|Thesaurus:libertine}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1977|author=w:Stevie Nicks|artist=w:Fleetwood Mac|title={{w|Dreams (Fleetwood Mac song)|Dreams}}|album=Rumours|publisher=Warner Bros.|passage=Thunder only happens when it’s rainin’ / '''Players''' only love you when they’re playin’ / Say women, they will come and they will go / When the rain washes you clean, you’ll know}}

